# CODEOWNERS — review gating for the paths where a mistake is either a
# security hole or invisible in review.
#
# Set @OWNERS to a real team slug or handle. A CODEOWNERS entry pointing at a
# team that does not exist is a silent no-op that reads like coverage, so this
# is deliberately not left as a placeholder: if you fork this repo, replace
# the handle with your own or with your org's team slug.
#
# Syntax: a trailing `/` on a directory pattern means "this directory and
# everything under it"; without it the pattern matches only the entry itself.

# ── Default: everything needs one review ────────────────────────────────────
*                              @davinakmalyasha

# ── HTTP surface ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every route, middleware chain, CORS/cookie decision and rate limit. A
# missing auth middleware or a wrong middleware ORDER is invisible in a diff
# review: the metrics-widdleware bug that 500'd every SSE endpoint looked
# correct in the diff and was wrong in production.
backend/internal/httpapi/            @davinakmalyasha
backend/internal/httpapi/handler/    @davinakmalyasha
backend/internal/httpapi/middleware/ @davinakmalyasha

# ── Money ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Webhook signature verification, capture/refund/dispute state transitions,
# idempotency, the commission split and the gateway adapters. A regression
# here is a financial incident, not a bug, and it does not look obviously
# wrong in a diff.
backend/internal/payments/           @davinakmalyasha
backend/internal/service/payment_service.go  @davinakmalyasha
backend/internal/service/order_service.go    @davinakmalyasha
backend/internal/repository/payment_repo.go  @davinakmalyasha

# ── Schema ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Migrations are applied by version and are effectively irreversible in
# practice: goose will not re-run a file, and a wrong index or a dropped
# column cannot be undone by reverting the commit. This is the one directory
# where "it looked fine" is not a sufficient review.
backend/internal/db/migrations/      @davinakmalyasha

# ── Auth & config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session/refresh handling, RBAC, the production guards and the secret
# deny-list.
backend/internal/config/             @davinakmalyasha
backend/internal/service/auth_service.go    @davinakmalyasha
backend/internal/service/token.go          @davinakmalyasha
backend/internal/service/oauth_service.go  @davinakmalyasha

# ── Background jobs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Order timeouts and sweeps move money and release inventory.
backend/internal/worker/             @davinakmalyasha
backend/cmd/                         @davinakmalyasha

# ── Client shared code ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# axios interceptors, the token/refresh single-flight, the HTML sanitizer, the
# SSE clients and the money formatting helpers. Everything else in web/src
# consumes these, so a change here has a blast radius far larger than the
# diff suggests.
web/src/lib/                         @davinakmalyasha
web/src/stores/                      @davinakmalyasha

# ── Infrastructure & CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
infra/                               @davinakmalyasha
.github/                             @davinakmalyasha
.gitleaks.toml                       @davinakmalyasha

# ── Container & proxy config ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# nginx `add_header` is NOT inherited into a location block that defines its
# own, so a header added at server level silently disappears on the HTML
# document. nginx.conf and the included header files are review-gated for that
# reason.
**/Dockerfile*                       @davinakmalyasha
web/nginx.conf                       @davinakmalyasha
web/nginx-brotli.conf                @davinakmalyasha
web/security-headers.conf            @davinakmalyasha
